{
  "summary": "This image-only ablation (ResNet50, single profile, no RNA, no fusion) achieved a validation accuracy of 0.208 (F1: 0.172), substantially below the RNA-only baseline (0.485) from llm_summary_001, indicating that under this minimal configuration the image modality alone carries far less predictive signal than RNA. Taken together with the multimodal result (0.527, llm_summary_002), the ablation triangle suggests the ~4.2-point multimodal gain over RNA-only is primarily attributable to the RNA component, with the image contributing a modest incremental signal on top rather than serving as an independently strong predictor. It remains uncertain whether a stronger image encoder (e.g., ViT-L), alternative fusion mechanisms, or multiprofile settings could substantially alter the image modality's contribution, and the very low image-only performance may reflect limitations of ResNet50 specifically rather than a fundamental lack of information in the image features."
}

